Let the merge's field values reach the formulas that depend on them.

cmd_merge_data_redo fills each new sheet's field cells with the low-level
gnm_cell_set_value, which neither queues the cell's dependents for
recalculation nor renders the cell: a formula in the merge zone that
reads a field (a greeting built from the name) keeps the value it got when
the zone was pasted with the fields still empty, and nothing marks it
dirty afterwards.  The GTK shows the right result only because its idle
redraw evaluates the pasted formulas after the fields are set.  Seen
through the Cocoa front end on 2026-10-13, where the sheet-added
notification renders earlier.  Use sheet_cell_set_value, the API that
queues the recalculation and the span, for both the value and the empty
case.

--- a/src/commands.c	2026-10-13 09:00:00
+++ b/src/commands.c	2026-10-13 09:00:00
@@ -5657,13 +5657,13 @@
 				GnmCell *target_cell = sheet_cell_get ((Sheet *)target_sheet->data,
 								      col_target, row_target);
 				if (target_cell != NULL)
-					gnm_cell_set_value (target_cell,
-							   value_new_empty ());
+					sheet_cell_set_value (target_cell,
+							      value_new_empty ());
 			} else {
 				GnmCell *target_cell = sheet_cell_fetch ((Sheet *)target_sheet->data,
 								      col_target, row_target);
-				gnm_cell_set_value (target_cell,
-						   value_dup (source_cell->value));
+				sheet_cell_set_value (target_cell,
+						      value_dup (source_cell->value));
 			}
 			target_sheet = target_sheet->next;
 			row_source++;
